  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Salient Crgt has $824M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, spread across 53 awards with an average award size of $15.5M. Obligations are up 0.9% year over year. General Services Administration is the largest buyer, accounting for $545M of obligations, followed by Department of Veterans Affairs with $136M and Department of Homeland Security with $52.3M. Computer Systems Design Services is the dominant market, with $735M in obligations, while Engineering Services accounts for $61.6M and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounts for $17.8M. Recent fiscal-year history shows steady growth in obligations: FY21 $240M, FY22 $405M, FY23 $505M, FY24 $557M, FY25 $816M, and FY26 $824M. This profile shows concentration in a small number of large awards and in a narrow range of NAICS markets and buying agencies, with the GSA and Computer Systems Design Services representing the largest shares of FY2026 to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Salient Crgt's FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "Salient Crgt's FY2026 obligations are highly concentrated. General Services Administration accounts for $545M of the $824M total and Computer Systems Design Services accounts for $735M of the $824M total. The top three agencies together represent the majority of obligations, with Department of Veterans Affairs at $136M and Department of Homeland Security at $52.3M following GSA."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has Salient Crgt's federal revenue trended recently?",
        "body": "Salient Crgt's obligations rose from $240M in FY21 to $824M in FY26. Obligations increased each reported year: FY21 $240M, FY22 $405M, FY23 $505M, FY24 $557M, FY25 $816M, FY26 $824M. Year over year obligations are up 0.9% in FY2026 to date."
      }
    ]
